diff --git a/packages/web/NOTES.md b/packages/web/NOTES.md
index 4da36e5..701031c 100644
--- a/packages/web/NOTES.md
+++ b/packages/web/NOTES.md
@@ -217,3 +217,51 @@ All logic is node-testable; `src/ui` and `main.ts` are covered by the e2e only.
   yielding with progress on the main thread, closed offline verifier CSP kept, no Worker). Option A needs a progress/yield hook in
   `@quietvote/protocol` `verifyElection` (owned by the #26 integration line); the page wiring follows once that hook lands.
   B3-26 is therefore open again; the verifier CSP is unchanged (no worker-src).
+
+## QV-ADR-027 web items: B3-06, B3-11a, B3-14, B3-25 (web side), B3-28 (2026-11-04)
+
+Owner-approved defaults from `docs/plan/DECISIONS-2026-11-04.md`. AI-assisted implementation, not an independent audit; QuietVote
+remains unaudited and not for real elections. Tests: `test/adr027.test.ts` (12 tests, negative cases included).
+
+* **B3-06 (option A, gated on STH freshness), `flow/pause.ts`:** the client derives PAUSED itself from control entries
+  `{proto, type: "control", action: "pause"|"resume", reason?}` (same closed schema as `logcheck.ts` CONTROL_RECORD) that carry
+  >= `coordinator.m` valid coordinator record signatures over sig-record(manifest_hash, "control", body). The manifest log
+  (operator) key never counts, even if a manifest lists it as a coordinator key (QV-ADR-022, QV-07-REQ-082 (c)). The v1 manifest
+  defines no trustee pause delegation, and the server and verifier accept only coordinator control records, so a trustee-signed
+  pause is not accepted (REQ-082 (b) needs a manifest field first). Only entries after election-open and before election-close
+  count; a resume ends a pause; a pause while paused or a resume while running is ignored, as in the server state machine.
+  `phase` becomes `paused` only when the current checkpoint is signed by the manifest log key under the manifest origin, its size
+  equals the number of entries read, its root equals the root recomputed from the entries' own headers (leaf computed only when
+  the header binds the body), and it has >= max(1, witness_quorum) cosignatures from manifest witnesses dated within the last
+  60 s (QV-07-REQ-041) and not more than 300 s ahead (QV-18 §9.3). Otherwise the pause is kept as `pauseSeq` with
+  `pauseConfirmed: false`: the vote form stays available and shows `qv.vote.pauseUnconfirmed`. A confirmed pause gets its own vote
+  screen (`qv.vote.paused`, `qv.vote.pausedBody`), checked before the closed/not-open screen, so PAUSED is never shown as closed.
+  The server's PAUSED refusal still maps to `E-API-UNAVAILABLE`, never `E-VOT-CLOSED`. The election load, the vote/spoils re-read
+  and the live layer read `GET .../log/checkpoint` after the entries. With a pause on record, the live layer also re-checks on
+  `witness` events and on reads without new entries, so a confirmation that has gone stale is dropped. Limits: elections whose
+  manifest names no witnesses can never confirm a pause (unconfirmed note only). Clock skew of the viewer's device moves the
+  60 s window. Control-record replay (B2-05 `control_seq`) is not checked here; if B2-05 adds a field to the closed schema, the
+  `CONTROL_RECORD` copy in `pause.ts` must follow.
+* **B3-11a (option A):** no code change. The 10 min idle lock (`key/lock.ts`) with its 2 min warning and "stay unlocked" is
+  accepted as QV-13-REQ-007 compliant; QV-13-REQ-007 and QV-19 §5.3 carry a marked note.
+* **B3-14 (option A):** guarantee 4 is chosen by the signed manifest (`isOneBallot`: `ballots.max_per_voter` = 1 →
+  `qv.privacy.g4single` "This election allows one ballot per person. Your first ballot counts."; otherwise the unchanged
+  `qv.privacy.g4`). The new key is a guarantee key (QV-10 §7.1 row added). The five draft catalogs carry machine-drafted text
+  because the catalog completeness test requires every key; no review record is added, so no translated locale is offered and they
+  all fall back to English. Not changed (outside the item): `qv.privacy.nc3` still mentions voting again.
+* **B3-25 (option A, web side), `key/passphrase.ts`:** `canonicalPassphrase` is the one shared KEK-input canonicalization, now
+  written into QV-19 §5.3. Exact definition for the CLI mirror:
+  `words = p.trim().toLowerCase().split(/[\s-]+/).filter((w) => w.length > 0)`; if `words.length >= 6` and every word is in the
+  embedded 1,296-word list (`key/wordlist.ts`) the form is `words.join(' ')`, else `p.normalize('NFKC')`; KEK input = UTF-8 of
+  that string. Wrap always uses it. `unlockPassphraseForms(p)` returns `[canonical]`, or `[canonical, p.normalize('NFKC')]` when the
+  two differ; `unwrapSeed` tries them in that order (at most two Argon2id runs, so a wrong word-list phrase costs two runs) and
+  `elapsedMs` times only the successful run, so calibration still measures one derivation. A container opened through the legacy
+  form and then re-wrapped at unlock (weaker than default) is re-wrapped under the canonical form. Until the CLI mirrors the
+  function, such a re-wrapped file or a web-created file opens in the CLI only with the canonical spelling. Legacy fixture: a
+  CLI-written container (`qv keygen`, phrase `LOBE-kuga-guna-husa-tejo-nula-neno`) unlocks with that exact phrase.
